MASTER RECEIPT ITEM EXTRACTION RULES
====================================

GOAL
----
For each purchased item, identify exactly:
- One Product Name
- One Final Item Price


LINE STRUCTURE RULES
====================

Preserve Line Order,
Receipt lines must be processed in their original top-to-bottom order.

Product and Price May Share a Line,
A product description and its final item price may occur on the same line.

Product and Price May Span Lines,
A product line without a final price may remain open while immediately following lines are examined for its final item price.

Following Lines Can Complete an Open Product,
When a probable product line has no final price, subsequent related lines should be examined before deciding that the product has no price.

Intermediate Lines Can Contain Pricing Mathematics,
Lines between a product name and its final price may contain unit prices, quantities, weights, or promotional calculations.


PRICE IDENTIFICATION RULES
==========================

Detect Price-Like Tokens,
A price-like token normally contains digits followed by a decimal separator and two decimal digits, such as 7.85, 14.29, 0.00, or $3.34.

Price-Like Does Not Mean Item Price,
A price-like token is only a candidate and must not automatically be treated as the final item price.

Distinguish Final Price from Price Components,
A line may contain multiple numeric or monetary values, and only one may represent the final item price.

Unit Price Is Not Necessarily Final Price,
A monetary value representing a unit price, such as price per pound, must not automatically be treated as the final item price.

Weight Is Not Final Price,
A numeric value representing product weight must not be treated as the final item price.

Quantity Is Not Final Price,
A numeric value representing quantity must not be treated as the final item price.

Promotional Price Is Not Necessarily Final Price,
A monetary value describing a promotion or deal must not automatically be treated as the final item price.

Savings Amount Is Not Final Price,
A monetary value representing savings or a discount must not be treated as the final item price.

Prefer Final Charge over Reference Amount,
When multiple monetary values are associated with an item, prefer the value representing the actual final charge rather than a unit price, promotional price, savings amount, or reference amount.

Zero Is a Valid Item Price,
A final item price of 0.00 is valid and must not be interpreted as a missing price.


POSITION RULES
==============

Use Price Position as Evidence,
A monetary value occupying the established item-price position or column is stronger evidence of the final item price than a monetary value embedded within descriptive or calculation text.

Price Position Is Not Absolute,
The position of a monetary value should be treated as evidence rather than absolute proof that it is the final item price.


PRODUCT ASSOCIATION RULES
=========================

Modifier Lines May Belong to Previous Product,
A line describing quantity, weight, promotion, discount, or price calculation may belong to the preceding product rather than representing another product.

Savings Lines Are Not Products,
A savings or discount line associated with a product must not generate a separate purchased item.

Do Not Create Items from Pricing Mathematics,
A line whose purpose is to explain the calculation of another item's price should not independently create a purchased item.


REPEATED PRODUCT RULES
======================

Repeated Product Names Are Valid,
Identical product descriptions may represent multiple independently purchased units.

Do Not Deduplicate by Product Name,
Repeated product descriptions must not automatically be merged or removed.

Each Independently Priced Occurrence Is an Item,
Each independently priced occurrence of a product should normally be retained as a separate purchased item.


FINAL OUTPUT RULES
==================

One Item Has One Final Price,
Regardless of how many source lines or numeric values participate in an item record, the normalized item must contain exactly one final item price.

One Item Has One Product Name,
Regardless of how many source lines participate in an item record, the normalized item must contain exactly one product name.

Preserve Ambiguity When Necessary,
If the available lines do not provide sufficient evidence to associate one final price with one product, preserve the ambiguity for later processing rather than inventing an association.